				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=346">Vandor</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">2/7/2001 - 2:52 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=311">Vandor Healstorm</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Hail all.<br />
<br />
   Ok From what I heard is alot of our members would like some help with quest for there Char. So I think i came up with a system that should work for all.  <br />
<br />
 1. Get the info on your Quest <br />
       Find out what you you need. There are tons of web pages that have a walk thru of    <br />
       most of the quest out there. So learn your quest inside and out. (what you need, who<br />
       to kill, what lvl they are, about how many players needed to take mob down and       where and when do they spawn)<br />
<br />
 2.  Do what you can on your own <br />
      Please do not arrange for help just to have some one sit there and wait for a low lvl<br />
      mob to spawn and kill it for part one of your quest when you really need help in the <br />
      second part. (Do the easy stuff first call for the backup when you really need it in the <br />
      quest)<br />
<br />
 3. Make a call to arms<br />
     Post a msg. on the board. State that you would like some help to do a quest. State<br />
     the quest, what part you need help with, how hard it is, and where and when you like        to do it. Have a sign up on msg board for players to state that they will help you on that      date and time. (Give yourself some time before the quest about a week that way you          know members could see it and make plains to help you then.)  <br />
<br />
 4. Look to get the most out of it.<br />
     Look at the othere Msg for help on board. Look at who might be able to get some thing      out of the same zone or near by zone. See if you can combine your request for help with      some one else.(Lets get the most out of it. Why wast a good group of members see if         you can get a few quest done  with one group call for help. Merge the quests.)<br />
<br />
 5. Do quest have fun<br />
     Thank the members that helped you out. look to return the favor.<br />
<br />
<br />
     Side notes<br />
<br />
 1. Be Real<br />
     Please do not state that you like to do your epic quest when you are lvl 32. Look at the <br />
     quest. Know the lvl of the quest your fellow guild mates around your lvl will be the ones      helping you. <br />
 <br />
  2. Give and Take<br />
     You should return the favor when you can, remember if you ask for help and do not give       any your fellow members will rember and stop helping you. Do not be greedy.<br />
<br />
  3. Why?<br />
      What I hope will happen is we will see a few groups of members. that will start to             form there own teams. They will learn how to work well with each other and work well       as a group when they are by there selfs helping each other or in a Raid.(This is a win          win situation for all...Form thos hunting tribes)<br />
<br />
<br />
<br />
ok there it is hope it works, hope you like it. if you have anything to add that you like or don't like state it.<br />
  Also its just a game....Have fun<br />
<br />
  Vandor						</td>
